<programme start="20261016203000 +0000" stop="20261016210000 +0000" channel="Food Network US"><title lang="en">Diners, Drive-Ins and Dives</title><sub-title lang="en">Lots of Latin</sub-title><desc lang="en">Guy Fieri is loading up on all kinds of Latin on this trip; in Logan, Utah, a Salvadoran spot puttin&apos; out pupusas and a cabeza creation.</desc><category lang="en">Travel</category><category lang="en">Food</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-G</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p185941_b_v12_cu.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261016210000 +0000" stop="20261016213000 +0000" channel="Food Network US"><title lang="en">Diners, Drive-Ins and Dives</title><sub-title lang="en">From Authentic to Inventive</sub-title><desc lang="en">Dishes from real deal to really creative; in Portland, Ore., a 70-year-old icon is serving up authentic Chinese recipes from the chef&apos;s hometown; a restaurant in Oklahoma City is cooking chicken and biscuits.</desc><category lang="en">Travel</category><category lang="en">Food</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-G</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p185941_b_v12_cu.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261016213000 +0000" stop="20261016220000 +0000" channel="Food Network US"><title lang="en">Diners, Drive-Ins and Dives</title><sub-title lang="en">Meat and Heat</sub-title><desc lang="en">Guy Fieri rolls into a tucked-away panini paradise in Chehalis, Wash.; a Korean spot in Brentwood, Tenn., gets spicy with its chicken and bulgogi; in Houston, a barbecue joint throws Tex-Mex into the mix with brisket tacos and jalapeño sausage.</desc><category lang="en">Travel</category><category lang="en">Food</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-G</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p185941_b_v12_cu.jpg"/></programme>
